# Code Conventions and Design Patterns

## Ruby Style Guide

This project follows Ruby best practices and conventions:

- Classes are defined in separate files under `lib/`
- File names use snake_case
- Test files are suffixed with `_spec.rb`
- Tests are organized by functionality
- Each class has a single responsibility

## Object-Oriented Design

The Mars Rover implementation uses these key OO principles:

1. **Single Responsibility Principle**
   - [position.rb](mdc:lib/position.rb) handles only position-related logic
   - [orientation.rb](mdc:lib/orientation.rb) manages only directional concerns
   - [mars_rover.rb](mdc:lib/mars_rover.rb) orchestrates the overall behavior

2. **Encapsulation**
   - Each class manages its own internal state
   - Public interfaces are clearly defined
   - Implementation details are hidden

## Testing Approach

- Tests are written using RSpec
- Organized by feature/functionality
- Follow the Given-When-Then pattern
- Use descriptive context blocks
- Test both happy path and edge cases
